1
00:00:00,418 --> 00:00:07,536
Workbench lets you correct an item's name, notes, and location while keeping its
permanent identity. This

2
00:00:07,536 --> 00:00:11,540
walkthrough uses a synthetic item and a disposable database.

3
00:00:12,945 --> 00:00:19,628
Open Edit details and change the name. Cancel returns to the saved record without
changing it.

4
00:00:21,042 --> 00:00:29,146
On a phone, change the location. This save encounters a simulated server failure.
Your text remains

5
00:00:29,146 --> 00:00:35,224
available, even when appearance changes. Retry safely submits the same checked
request.

6
00:00:36,636 --> 00:00:43,324
Two independently signed-in sessions opened the same record. The other session now
saves a new name.

7
00:00:43,324 --> 00:00:48,758
Saving this older draft reports a conflict and preserves the draft for comparison.

8
00:00:50,163 --> 00:00:57,017
Review my edits starts from the latest saved values. Keep the new name, copy the
intended

9
00:00:57,017 --> 00:01:03,015
notes from the preserved draft, and save. The newer record is never silently
overwritten.

10
00:01:04,425 --> 00:01:11,163
Return to the collection and search the updated notes. The same item appears with its
corrected

11
00:01:11,163 --> 00:01:14,953
name and location. Reloading confirms the changes are stored.
